{
  "id": "u08-l08",
  "unit": "u08-daily-routine",
  "title": "I can, I think",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**Can** = infinitive + **পারা**: বলতে **পারি** \"I can speak\", বলতে **পারেন** \"you can speak\", খেতে **পারি না** \"I can't eat\". You already know the chunk **বুঝতে পারছি না** — that is the same verb.\n\nTo give an opinion, start with **(আমার) মনে হয়** \"I think\" (lit. \"it comes to my mind\"). **হয়তো** \"maybe\" softens a guess.\n\nIn class: **আমার একটা প্রশ্ন আছে** \"I have a question\".",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "bolte",
      "bn": "বলতে",
      "tr": "bolte",
      "en": "to speak",
      "notes": "Infinitive of বলা, like খেতে from খাওয়া."
    },
    {
      "id": "pari",
      "bn": "পারি",
      "tr": "pari",
      "en": "(I) can",
      "notes": "Infinitive + পারা = \"can\": বলতে পারি \"I can speak\". Negative: পারি না \"I can't\"."
    },
    {
      "id": "paren",
      "bn": "পারেন",
      "tr": "paren",
      "en": "(you, polite) can"
    },
    {
      "id": "pare",
      "bn": "পারে",
      "tr": "pare",
      "en": "(he/she) can"
    },
    {
      "id": "mone-hoy",
      "bn": "মনে হয়",
      "tr": "mone hoy",
      "en": "I think",
      "notes": "Lit. \"it comes to mind\". Often with আমার: আমার মনে হয় \"I think\"."
    },
    {
      "id": "hoyto",
      "bn": "হয়তো",
      "tr": "hoyto",
      "en": "maybe"
    },
    {
